  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to `Arbeidstilsynet.Saksarkiv.Client` are documented in this file.\n\nThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and this project\nadheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html). While on `0.x`, minor\nversions may contain breaking changes.\n\nEvery released version must have a `## <version>` heading matching `<Version>` in\n`Saksarkiv.Client.csproj`; CI fails otherwise.\n\n## [Unreleased]\n\n## 0.1.0-beta.1\n\nFirst version, replacing `Arbeidstilsynet.Common.Saksarkiv` (from\n[dotnet-common](https://github.com/Arbeidstilsynet/dotnet-common)), now published from this\nrepository.\n\n### Added\n\n- `SaksarkivClientV3` in `Arbeidstilsynet.Saksarkiv.Client.V3`, generated for API v3.\n- `OpprettSakAsync(...)` extension and `SaksarkivFile` for creating a case with files over v3.\n- `AddSaksarkivClientV3(...)`.\n- The OpenAPI documents (`openApiV2.json`, `openApiV3.json`) are included in the package.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Package renamed from `Arbeidstilsynet.Common.Saksarkiv` to `Arbeidstilsynet.Saksarkiv.Client`,\n  and the root namespace from `Arbeidstilsynet.Common.Saksarkiv` to\n  `Arbeidstilsynet.Saksarkiv.Client`.\n- The v2 client is renamed from `SaksarkivClient` to `SaksarkivClientV2` and moved to\n  `Arbeidstilsynet.Saksarkiv.Client.V2`. Register it with `AddSaksarkivClientV2(...)` (previously\n  `AddSaksarkivClient(...)`).\n- The clients are generated at build time from the OpenAPI documents produced by\n  Saksarkivtjeneste, instead of a copy of the document. For v2 this means:\n  - Model namespaces gained an `AT.EArkiv` segment, e.g. `V2.Models.AT.EArkiv.Entiteter.Meldinger`\n    (previously `Models.Entiteter.Meldinger`).\n  - `Apiv2.Sak.Validersaksnummer` is split into `ValiderSaksnummer` (`POST`) and\n    `ValidersaksnummerEscaped` (`GET`).\n  - `Apiv2.Saker.FinnMedReferanser` accepts the `KunUtgaatteSaker` query parameter.\n  - `Apiv2.Health.ArkivStatus` and `Api.Health.Ping`/`AuthPing` are available.\n- Unsafe HTTP methods (`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`, `CONNECT`) are no longer retried.\n  Previously only `POST` was excluded.\n- Retries for the health probe are also skipped when the request fails with an exception.\n- The `Saksarkiv` health check is registered by both `AddSaksarkivClientV2(...)` and\n  `AddSaksarkivClientV3(...)`, and only once when both are called.\n- Targets `net10.0` only (previously also `net8.0`).",
  "repository": {
